This licence covers the code in this repository: `reference/`, `tests/`,
`tools/`, and `.github/`.

The prose and diagrams — `README.md` and everything under `docs/` — are
licensed CC-BY-4.0 instead; see `LICENSE-docs`.

The split is deliberate. Creative Commons itself recommends against using its
licences for software: they carry no patent grant, and their terms are written
for text rather than for something that gets compiled and shipped. A repository
whose subject is licence hygiene should not be the one place where a text
licence is stretched over Python.
